---
title: "Quick Access Toolbar"
enterprise: true
---

The Toolbar appears above the grid and provides quick access to common grid actions. It supports built-in items, custom components, and configurable ordering and alignment.

Configure the Toolbar with the `toolbar` grid option. The property takes a list of Toolbar Items.

{% apiDocumentation source="grid-options/properties.json" section="accessories" names=["toolbar"] /%}

{% gridExampleRunner title="Built-in Items" name="built-in-items" exampleHeight=590 /%}

```{% frameworkTransform=true %}
const gridOptions = {
    toolbar: {
        alignment: 'right',
        items: [
            { toolbarItem: 'find', alignment: 'left' },
            'autoSizeAll',
            'separator',
            'csvExport',
            'excelExport',
            'separator',
            { toolbarItem: 'resetColumns', display: 'iconAndLabel' },
        ]
    },

    // other grid options ...
}
```

## Built-in Items

The following built-in items are available as string shorthands:

-   `autoSizeAll`: Auto-sizes all columns to fit their content. Requires `ColumnAutoSizeModule`.
-   `columnChooser`: Opens the Column Chooser dialog. Requires `ColumnMenuModule`.
-   `columnsPanel`: Toggles the Columns Tool Panel in the sidebar. Requires `SideBarModule` and `ColumnsToolPanelModule`. Hidden if the sidebar does not include a columns panel.
-   `csvExport`: Exports grid data as CSV. Requires `CsvExportModule`.
-   `excelExport`: Exports grid data as Excel. Requires `ExcelExportModule`.
-   `filtersPanel`: Toggles the Filters Tool Panel in the sidebar. Requires `SideBarModule` and `FiltersToolPanelModule`. Hidden if the sidebar does not include a filters panel.
-   `find`: A text input that searches within grid cells using the Find feature. Displays the current match count and provides Previous/Next navigation buttons. Use Enter to navigate to the next match and Shift+Enter for the previous match. Requires `FindModule`.
-   `pivotPanel`: Embeds the Pivot Panel in the toolbar. Requires `RowGroupingPanelModule`. Configured independently of the `pivotPanelShow` grid option — if both are set, both will render.
-   `rowGroupPanel`: Embeds the Row Group Panel in the toolbar. Requires `RowGroupingPanelModule`. Configured independently of the `rowGroupPanelShow` grid option — if both are set, both will render.
-   `quickFilter`: A text input that filters grid rows using the Quick Filter. Requires `QuickFilterModule`.
-   `resetColumns`: Resets all columns to their default state.

Built-in items require their corresponding modules to be registered. If a required module is not registered, the item will not render and a console warning will be logged.

## Configuration

Items are rendered in the order they are defined.

The `alignment` property can be `left` or `right`. When not set on an item, it falls back to the toolbar-level `alignment`, which itself defaults to `left` in LTR and `right` in RTL.

The `key` uniquely identifies a Toolbar Item.

Additional props are passed to Toolbar Items using `toolbarItemParams`.

```{% frameworkTransform=true %}
const gridOptions = {
    toolbar: {
        items: [
            'autoSizeAll',
            {
                key: 'myItem',
                toolbarItem: CustomToolbarComponent,
                alignment: 'right',
                toolbarItemParams: {
                    label: 'Custom Label'
                }
            }
        ]
    }
}
```

### Default Alignment

Set `alignment` at the toolbar level to change the default for every item that does not specify its own alignment. When omitted, items default to `left` in LTR and `right` in RTL.

```{% frameworkTransform=true %}
const gridOptions = {
    toolbar: {
        alignment: 'right',
        items: [
            'find',
            { toolbarItem: 'autoSizeAll', alignment: 'left' },
        ]
    }
}
```

### Display Mode

Items can be displayed as icons only (default) or icons with labels. Set the `display` property at the toolbar level or per item. Item-level settings take precedence.

```{% frameworkTransform=true %}
const gridOptions = {
    toolbar: {
        display: 'iconAndLabel',
        items: [
            'autoSizeAll',
            { toolbarItem: 'csvExport', display: 'icon' }
        ]
    }
}
```

## Custom Components

In addition to the built-in items, the Toolbar can render Custom Components. Use a Custom Component when the built-in items do not cover your use case, for example to trigger application-specific actions, surface a bespoke control, or reflect external state.

A Custom Toolbar Item is passed via the `toolbarItem` property of a Toolbar Item definition, alongside an optional `key`, `alignment`, `display` and `toolbarItemParams` object for passing custom props.

```{% frameworkTransform=true %}
const gridOptions = {
    toolbar: {
        items: [
            {
                key: 'analyseByCountry',
                toolbarItem: CustomToolbarItem,
                toolbarItemParams: { /* any custom props */ },
            },
        ],
    },
}
```

Custom Toolbar Item components implement the `IToolbarItemComp` interface. The component is responsible for creating its own DOM via `init(params)` / `getGui()`, cleaning up in `destroy()`, and optionally implementing `refresh(params)` to handle toolbar updates in place — returning `true` keeps the existing instance, while returning `false` (or omitting the method) causes the grid to destroy and recreate the item. Params passed to the component include the grid `api`, the item `key`, the resolved `display` mode, and any values supplied via `toolbarItemParams`.

The example below demonstrates a Custom Toolbar Item that toggles a row grouping and filter state when clicked, using the grid API made available through the component params:

